-- title:
--   Linear forms vanishing in J² on a Drinfeld chart have coefficients in I
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime number, $W$ a commutative ring, $I \subseteq W$ an ideal and $t \in I$. Let $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ be formal power series in two variables such that $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1)$ lies in the $(q+2)$-nd power of the ideal $(X_0, X_1)$, where $X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ is the Drinfeld form `drinfeldForm` over $W$. Let $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,2 \to W$ be a pair of elements of $W$, and write $\pi$ for the quotient map of $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the principal ideal generated by the single relation $C(t)\,v - f\,u$. Assume that the image under $\pi$ of the linear form $\sum_{i} C(a_i)X_i$ lies in the square of the ideal generated by $\pi(X_0)$ and $\pi(X_1)$. Then $a_i \in I$ for both $i$. Note that the hypothesis on $f$ is used only through the weaker consequence that $f \in (X_0,X_1)^2$.
--
--   A uniqueness statement for linear parts on the Drinfeld local chart of a modular curve in the shape of Katz–Mazur: two candidate linear parts of one endomorphism of the chart, read off modulo the square of the ideal generated by the coordinates, agree entrywise modulo $I$ (applied with $I$ the maximal ideal of $W$ and $t$ the relevant chart parameter). It is used in the linear-part transport statements [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.exists_semilinear_linearPart_transport_of_forall_specialLinearGroup_of_dense) and its prime variant, and in the full-level auxiliary computation [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.linearPart_row_mem_maximalIdeal_of_coeffMap_of_drinfeldChartWitness_anchor_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.linearPart_row_mem_maximalIdeal_of_coeffMap_of_drinfeldChartWitness_anchor_twoChartIntegralModel_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd).
